.TH LIBMPQ__BLOCK_SIZE_PACKED 3 2026-09-11 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__block_size_packed \- query the stored size of one data block
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__block_size_packed("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive",
.BI "        uint32_t       " "file_number",
.BI "        uint32_t       " "block_number",
.BI "        libmpq__off_t *" "size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Return the stored byte size of the selected logical block. For sectorized
COMPRESS or IMPLODE files, this is the difference between consecutive
sector offsets. The reader loads and, when necessary, decrypts the offset
table internally. No payload decoding or checksum verification is performed.
.PP
Raw blocks use their logical byte count, including the final partial sector.
Single-unit files have one block whose size is the file's stored packed size.
Encryption does not change the reported size. Offset-table bytes and sector
checksum-table bytes are excluded, including from the final data block.
.PP
This complements libmpq__block_size_unpacked(), which reports decoded bytes.
Use the unpacked size when allocating a buffer for libmpq__block_read().
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns LIBMPQ_SUCCESS and stores the size in *size on success.
A non-NULL size output is initialized to zero before validation and remains
zero on failure. LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates NULL required arguments or an
invalid file/block index. LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED indicates a writer
archive. Malformed offsets, out-of-range payloads, table I/O, decryption and
allocation failures retain the existing reader's negative error codes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__block_size_unpacked (3),
.BR libmpq__block_compression (3),
.BR libmpq__file_size_packed (3),
.BR libmpq__block_read (3),
.BR libmpq__block_verify (3)
